  "knowledge": {
    "progressSummary": "COMPLETE: 156-line Lean file, 5 theorems, 0 sorries, 0 axioms. Proved gauss_sum_sq_corrected (direct from Mathlib's gaussSum_sq), legendreSym_eq_quadChar, legendre_gauss_sum_sq, parent_axiom_is_false (parent axiom is false for all odd primes), gauss_sum_analysis. PR pending.",
    "insights": [
      "Parent OQ-02 axiom gauss_sum_sq (claiming \u03c4 : \u2124) is mathematically FALSE for all odd primes p: \u03c4\u00b2 = p requires p to be a perfect square (impossible for primes), \u03c4\u00b2 = -p requires negative \u03c4\u00b2 (impossible).",
      "The CORRECT statement: gaussSum \u03c7 \u03c8 ^ 2 = \u03c7(-1) * p in R', where \u03c4 = gaussSum \u03c7 \u03c8 lives in the codomain R', not \u2124.",
      "Mathlib.NumberTheory.GaussSum provides gaussSum_sq directly, covering the abstract case. No cyclotomic field infrastructure needed for the abstract proof.",
      "legendreSym p a = quadraticChar (ZMod p) a is a definitional equality (rfl), making the Legendre symbol connection trivial.",
      "neg_one_pow_eq_or : \u2200 n : \u2115, (-1 : R)^n = 1 \u2228 (-1 : R)^n = -1 (from Mathlib.Algebra.Ring.Commute) is the key lemma for the case analysis in parent_axiom_is_false."
    ],
    "builtItems": [
      "gauss_sum_sq_corrected: gaussSum \u03c7 \u03c8 ^ 2 = \u03c7(-1) * (p : R') [ElementaryQuadraticReciprocityOQ02OQ01.lean:68]",
      "legendreSym_eq_quadChar: legendreSym p a = quadraticChar (ZMod p) a [line 83]",
      "legendre_gauss_sum_sq: Gauss sum formula for Legendre char via ring hom \u03c6 : \u2124 \u2192+* R' [line 89]",
      "parent_axiom_is_false: \u00ac \u2203 \u03c4 : \u2124, \u03c4\u00b2 = (-1)^(p/2) * p for odd primes [line 108]",
